  "term": "methoxyhydroxyphenylglycol",
  "definition": "Methoxyhydroxyphenylglycol is a substance produced in the body from epinephrine and norepinephrine. It can be measured in the brain, blood, cerebrospinal fluid, and urine, and its levels are used as an indicator of catecholamine turnover.",
